      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Think of the Fourier Transform as a lens that determines how much of a signal's energy is concentrated at different frequencies. Imagine a fingerprint left in a dusty room - you can measure how much dust settles around each finger print, roughly indicating the shape and size of the imprint at that point. Similarly, the Fourier Transform shows you where the 'fingerprints' of energy signatures in your signal are located, essentially revealing its component frequencies.",
