      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Fourier Transform doesn't literally \"pull them apart\", but rather finds the \"frequencies with the most amplitude\" in the mixed wave pattern, effectively organizing the components by frequency. Think of it as sorting the train of waves into separate tracks, not ripping them apart. The process does involve the concept of filtering, where a periodic filter is used in the frequency domain to isolate individual frequencies.",
      "source": "target",
